  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="3402-761d-c347-8437" name="Xiongnu (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #36 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). 200 BC to 200 AD These peoples formed a number of tribes living in Mongolia on the borders of China. By 200 BC they had formed a powerful confederation and were able to amass sizeable armies; they posed such a problem to the Chinese that what became the Great Wall was started to contain them. Relations between the states oscillated between war and a peace based on bribery for a considerable period. There is a theory that part of the Xiongnu migrated westward and became known to Europeans as the Huns. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Xiongnu]
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: At least 50% Infantry: Up to 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: none</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
